* NickLink v1.3 power rail from +5V down (values from tools/spec.py). C12 (+5V, 10u 0603) is
* instantiated by each testbench so hot-plug can use the bias-dependent model.
* Param C5 = nominal 3V3 bulk (C5 10u 0603 as built; only the hot-plug fix study changes it).
* p5 = +5V (J1.1, C12, U2 IN/EN), p3 = +3.3V, p3a = +3.3VA.
* Soft-start node for .ic: v(<inst>.xu2.u1_n08530)=0 (see parts.lib header).
.subckt NL_RAIL p5 p3 p3a params: C5=10u
XU2 p5 0 p5 p3 nc TLV75533P_TRANS
XC8 p3 0 C1U0402
XC5 p3 0 MLCC C0={C5} V0=3.65 ESR=5m ESL=0.5n VB=3.3
XC1 p3 0 C100N0402
XC2 p3 0 C100N0402
XC3 p3 0 C100N0402
XC4 p3 0 C100N0402
XC14 p3 0 C100N0402
XC15 p3 0 C100N0402
XFB1 p3 p3a BLM15AG121
XC6 p3a 0 C100N0402
XC7 p3a 0 C1U0402
* Power LED D1 + R3 (always on, ~1 mA)
D1 p3 led_k LED_R_TYP
R3 led_k 0 1.5k
.ends NL_RAIL

* Current spec.py rail (after the hot-plug rework): no C5; C4 4.7 uF 0402 X5R 10 V at VDD3
* (V0 = 3.1 assumed, 47 % at 3.3 V); C1-C3, C14, C15 100 nF; C8 1 uF; FB1 + C6/C7; D1 + R3.
* C12 (4.7 uF 0402 on VSYS) is instantiated by the testbench. p5 = VSYS.
.subckt NL_RAIL_V13 p5 p3 p3a
XU2 p5 0 p5 p3 nc TLV75533P_TRANS
XC8 p3 0 C1U0402
XC4 p3 0 MLCC C0=4.7u V0=3.1 ESR=10m ESL=0.3n VB=3.3
XC1 p3 0 C100N0402
XC2 p3 0 C100N0402
XC3 p3 0 C100N0402
XC14 p3 0 C100N0402
XC15 p3 0 C100N0402
XFB1 p3 p3a BLM15AG121
XC6 p3a 0 C100N0402
XC7 p3a 0 C1U0402
D1 p3 led_k LED_R_TYP
R3 led_k 0 1.5k
.ends NL_RAIL_V13
